The general estimate remains unproved. I proved for XX, every even \(L\ge4\) and all \(\beta\ge0\),
\[
R_L(\beta)\le 2\log2+\frac{5\pi}{3}\frac{\beta}{L}.
\]
This gives \(k=10\pi/3\), \(f(2)=1\). I also proved \(R_L\le\log d\) for diagonal classical chains.

The general arguments encounter explicit obstructions: seam averaging retains an \(O(M)\) norm, \(R_L\) is neither convex nor concave, and the information identity contains marginal relative entropies that dimension alone cannot bound.

Full-trace checks cover XX through paired length 8192, Heisenberg through length 8, and SU(3) through length 6. Larger interacting runs are SLURM-ready but unsubmitted.

Derivations and limitations are in [PROOF.md](PROOF.md), with the summary in [RESULT.md](RESULT.md) and numerical findings in [CHECKS.md](CHECKS.md).

